 "capability": "hto",
 "title": "Hashtag demultiplexing (HTO)",
 "conclusion": "On the public Howitt et al. 2023 hashing benchmark with genotype truth, Singlet's hashtag calls reach mean F-scores of 0.919, 0.814, 0.752, 0.742 while calling few genetic doublets singlets; it does not beat the best competitor on every batch (see failing metrics).",
 "methods": "Data: Howitt et al. 2023 (Zenodo 8304003): paediatric bronchoalveolar lavage, 3 batches of 8 genetically distinct donors with 8 TotalSeq-A hashtags (2 captures each), and 3 lung cancer cell lines with MULTI-seq lipid tags (3 captures). Truth: vireo genetic donor per cell (cellSNP-lite on 1000 Genomes common SNPs), including genetic doublets; donor i is hashtag i. As in the paper, each method runs on each capture separately on the called cells (no empty droplets are available), and the F-score per hashtag is tp / (tp + (fp + fn) / 2) over all cells of the dataset, averaged over hashtags; the second metric is the share of genetic doublets called a singlet. HTODemux and MULTIseqDemux (Seurat 5.5.1) and hashsolo (scanpy 1.12.4) were run here at their defaults; the other competitors are the paper's own calls, and re-scoring them with this code reproduces the paper's Table 1. Singlet's caller is singlet.adt.hto.call_hashtags.",
 "status": "final",
 "generated_at": "2026-10-25T14:46:10+00:00",
